cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TamerOp in your research, please cite this software and record
  the version or Git commit used for your analysis.
type: software
title: "TamerOp.jl: Toolkit for Algebraic Module Encodings over R^n and Other Posets"
authors:
  - family-names: Novak
    given-names: Erik
repository-code: "https://github.com/erikmnovak/TamerOp.jl"
url: "https://github.com/erikmnovak/TamerOp.jl"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TamerOp stands for Toolkit for Algebraic Module Encodings over R^n and
  Other Posets. It began as an implementation of Ezra Miller's Homological
  algebra of modules over posets, and finite encoding remains its organizing
  mathematical idea. The name also recalls tameness, the finiteness condition
  linking encodings, indicator presentations, and resolutions in that theory.
  The library constructs finite-poset models from supported data and
  mathematical presentations, retaining vector spaces, structure maps,
  and their relationship to the original parameter domain. These encoded
  objects support module algebra, derived computations, invariants,
  feature extraction, and visualization, with explicit mathematical scope.
keywords:
  - finite encodings
  - finite posets
  - tame modules
  - persistence modules
  - multiparameter persistence
  - computational topology
  - homological algebra
  - Julia
